From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:18:16 +0200
Subject: Seal package-object prefixes on implicit candidate references

An extension method or conversion provided by a top-level given, found via
implicit search, is referenced with a bare-package prefix. asSeenFrom then
leaves the defining package object's ThisType in the method's result type,
and a ThisType prefix is exactly what makes a top-level opaque alias
transparent, so the underlying type's members leak wherever the result
flows: proscenium's chained cons on its opaque List resolved the outer ::
to the underlying sci.List member (soundness#1809). Upstream #21527 fixed
this family for identifiers by sealing prefixes in findRef; typedImplicit
now does the same for search candidates. Present in stock Scala 3.7.4 and
3.8.3; upstream candidate.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude); two-polarity reproduction in the
feature documentation.

Enabled by `-Z:given-prefixes`; without it, upstream's code runs at every site this
patch touches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: givenprefix
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Implicits.scala | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Implicits.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Implicits.scala
index 67f94ef192a4dffa042b6541b20a2ad62522edd8..17f23ee05a105e39d87a5120ac1c848d0765de5d 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Implicits.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Implicits.scala
@@ -1170,7 +1170,17 @@ trait Implicits:
     if ctx.run.nn.isCancelled then NoMatchingImplicitsFailure
     else
       record("typedImplicit")
-      val ref = cand.ref
+      // Give the ref an explicit package-object prefix so that asSeenFrom
+      // rewrites the package object's ThisType in its member types. Otherwise
+      // an extension method or conversion defined in a package object and
+      // returning an opaque type of that package object would have a result
+      // type in which the opaque alias stays transparent. `findRef` does the
+      // same for identifiers.
+      val ref =
+        if !config.Proscala.enabled(config.Proscala.GivenPrefixes) then cand.ref
+        else cand.ref.makePackageObjPrefixExplicit match
+          case ref: TermRef => ref
+          case _ => cand.ref
       val generated: Tree = tpd.ref(ref).withSpan(span.startPos)
       val locked = ctx.typerState.ownedVars
       val adapted =
